[47.770258, "o", "   361\t**Exit codes:**\r\n   362\t- `0`: Success.\r\n   363\t- `2`: Error (invalid arguments, missing or malformed files, validation failure).\r\n   364\t\r\n   365\t### 5.2 Compare Command\r\n   366\t\r\n"]
[47.770375, "o", "   367\t```\r\n   368\tmlreport compare --baseline <path> --candidate <path> --config <path> --output-dir <path> [--format md|json|both]\r\n   369\t```\r\n   370\t\r\n   371\t- `--baseline` (required): Path to baseline evaluation manifest.\r\n   372\t- `--candidate` (required): Path to candidate evaluation manifest.\r\n   373\t- `--config` (required): Path to regression configuration JSON file.\r\n   374\t- `--output-dir` (required): Directory for output files. Created if it does not exist.\r\n   375\t- `--format` (optional, default `both`): Output format.\r\n   376\t\r\n   377\t**Validation:**\r\n   378\t- Baseline and candidate must have the same `task_type`.\r\n   379\t- Baseline and candidate must have the same set of split names.\r\n   380\t- If validation fails, exit with code 2 and print an error message to stderr.\r\n   381\t\r\n   382\t**Output files:**\r\n"]
[47.770505, "o", "   383\t- `<output-dir>/comparison.md` (when format is `md` or `both`)\r\n   384\t- `<output-dir>/comparison.json` (when format is `json` or `both`)\r\n   385\t\r\n   386\t**Exit codes:**\r\n   387\t- `0`: No regression detected (overall PASS).\r\n   388\t- `1`: Regression detected (overall FAIL).\r\n   389\t- `2`: Error.\r\n   390\t\r\n   391\t"]
[47.770584, "o", "### 5.3 Error Output\r\n   392\t\r\n   393\tAll error messages are printed to stderr. On error, no output files are created.\r\n   394\tError messages should be descriptive and include the file path and the nature of the problem.\r\n   395\t\r\n   396\t---\r\n   397\t\r\n   398\t## 6. Numeric Formatting\r\n   399\t\r\n   400\t- All metric values in reports are rounded to **6 decimal places**.\r\n   401\t- Relative deltas in comparison reports are shown as percentages rounded to **2 decimal places**.\r\n   402\t- Confusion matrix counts are integers (no decimal places).\r\n   403\t- Support counts are integers.\r\n"]
[47.771023, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
