[54.586586, "o", "nl -ba docs/spec_v1.md | sed -n '100,180p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[54.590062, "o", "   100\t### 2.3 Per-Metric Regression Evaluation\r\n   101\t\r\n   102\tFor each split in both baseline and candidate manifests:\r\n   103\t\r\n   104\t1. Compute all metrics for both baseline and candidate on that split.\r\n   105\t2. For each metric defined in `thresholds`:\r\n   106\t   a. Compute `absolute_delta = candidate_value - baseline_value`.\r\n"]
[54.590281, "o", "   107\t   b. Compute `relative_delta = (candidate_value - baseline_value) / |baseline_value|` if `|baseline_value| > 1e-10`, else skip relative check.\r\n   108\t   c. The metric is regressed on this split if `absolute_delta < min_absolute_delta` OR `relative_delta < min_relative_delta` (when relative check is applicable).\r\n   109\t3. A metric is counted toward the severity bucket if it regresses on **any** split.\r\n   110\t4. Each metric counts at most once toward its severity bucket regardless of how many splits it regresses on.\r\n   111\t\r\n   112\t---\r\n   113\t\r\n   114\t## 3. Metric Computation\r\n   115\t\r\n   116\t### 3.1 Binary Classification\r\n   117\t\r\n   118\t**Positive class convention:** The positive class is the class label that comes **last** in case-insensitive lexicographic order. For example, between `\"negative\"` and `\"positive\"`, `\"positive\"` is the positive class. Between `\"benign\"` and `\"malignant\"`, `\"malignant\"` is positive.\r\n   119\t\r\n"]
[54.590368, "o", "   120\t**Confusion matrix** from raw predictions using the `predicted` field:\r\n   121\t- TP: `actual == positive_class AND predicted == positive_class`\r\n   122\t- FP: `actual == negative_class AND predicted == positive_class`\r\n   123\t- FN: `actual == positive_class AND predicted == negative_class`\r\n   124\t- TN: `actual == negative_class AND predicted == negative_class`\r\n   125\t\r\n   126\t**Metrics** (all rounded to 6 decimal places in output):\r\n   127\t\r\n   128\t| Metric | Formula | Division-by-zero handling |\r\n   129\t|--------|---------|--------------------------|\r\n   130\t| `accuracy` | `(TP + TN) / (TP + TN + FP + FN)` | Return 0.0 if denominator is 0 |\r\n   131\t| `precision` | `TP / (TP + FP)` | Return 0.0 if denominator is 0 |\r\n   132\t| `recall` | `TP / (TP + FN)` | Return 0.0 if denominator is 0 |\r\n   133\t| `f1` | `2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall)` | Return 0.0 if denominator is 0 |\r\n   134\t| `auc_roc` | Trapezoidal AUC over ROC curve (see below) | Requires at least one positive and one negative sa"]
[54.590544, "o", "mple; return 0.0 otherwise |\r\n   135\t| `log_loss` | `-1/N * sum(y*ln(p) + (1-y)*ln(1-p))` | Clip probabilities to `[1e-15, 1-1e-15]` before log |\r\n   136\t\r\n   137\t**AUC-ROC computation:**\r\n   138\t\r\n   139\t1. Let `p_i` be the probability of the positive class for sample `i`.\r\n   140\t2. Sort all samples by `p_i` in **descending** order. Break ties by placing actual-positive samples before actual-negative samples (this ensures a consistent curve).\r\n   141\t3. Walk through sorted samples, tracking cumulative TP and FP counts.\r\n   142\t4. At each sample, compute `TPR = cumulative_TP / total_positives` and `FPR = cumulative_FP / total_negatives`.\r\n   143\t5. Compute AUC using the trapezoidal rule: `AUC = sum over consecutive points: (FPR_{i+1} - FPR_i) * (TPR_{i+1} + TPR_i) / 2`.\r\n   144\t6. Include the origin point `(0, 0)` at the start.\r\n   145\t\r\n   146\t### 3.2 Multiclass Classification\r\n   147\t\r\n   148\t**Class list:** Collect all unique class labels from `actual` values, sorted in case-insensitive lexicographic orde"]
[54.59066, "o", "r.\r\n   149\t\r\n   150\t**Per-class metrics (one-vs-rest):**\r\n   151\tFor each class `c`:\r\n   152\t- TP_c: `actual == c AND predicted == c`\r\n   153\t- FP_c: `actual != c AND predicted == c`\r\n   154\t- FN_c: `actual == c AND predicted != c`\r\n   155\t- TN_c: `actual != c AND predicted != c`\r\n   156\t- Precision_c, Recall_c, F1_c computed as in binary.\r\n   157\t\r\n   158\t**Aggregate metrics:**\r\n   159\t\r\n   160\t| Aggregate | Definition |\r\n   161\t|-----------|------------|\r\n   162\t| `accuracy` | Total correct predictions / total predictions |\r\n   163\t| `precision_micro` | `sum(TP_c) / sum(TP_c + FP_c)` over all classes |\r\n   164\t| `recall_micro` | `sum(TP_c) / sum(TP_c + FN_c)` over all classes |\r\n   165\t| `f1_micro` | `2 * precision_micro * recall_micro / (precision_micro + recall_micro)` |\r\n   166\t| `precision_macro` | Arithmetic mean of per-class precisions |\r\n   167\t| `recall_macro` | Arithmetic mean of per-class recalls |\r\n   168\t| `f1_macro` | Arithmetic mean of per-class F1 scores |\r\n   169\t| `precision_weighted` | Wei"]
[54.590766, "o", "ghted mean of per-class precisions, weighted by class support |\r\n   170\t| `recall_weighted` | Weighted mean of per-class recalls, weighted by class support |\r\n   171\t| `f1_weighted` | Weighted mean of per-class F1 scores, weighted by class support |\r\n   172\t\r\n   173\tWhere **support** for class `c` is the count of samples where `actual == c`.\r\n   174\t\r\n   175\tDivision-by-zero: return 0.0 for any metric where the denominator is 0.\r\n   176\t\r\n   177\t### 3.3 Regression Metrics\r\n   178\t\r\n   179\tAll metrics computed from arrays of `actual` and `predicted` numeric values:\r\n   180\t\r\n"]
[54.591132, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
