[1992.143925, "o", "Where **support** for class `c` is the count of samples where `actual == c`.\r\n\r\nDivision-by-zero: return 0.0 for any metric where the denominator is 0.\r\n\r\n### 3.3 Regression Metrics\r\n\r\n"]
[1992.144033, "o", "All metrics computed from arrays of `actual` and `predicted` numeric values:\r\n\r\n| Metric | Formula | Notes |\r\n|--------|---------|-------|\r\n| `mse` | `mean((actual_i - predicted_i)^2)` | |\r\n| `rmse` | `sqrt(mse)` | |\r\n| `mae` | `mean(\\|actual_i - predicted_i\\|)` | |\r\n| `r_squared` | `1 - SS_res / SS_tot` | `SS_res = sum((actual - predicted)^2)`, `SS_tot = sum((actual - mean(actual))^2)`. Return 0.0 if `SS_tot == 0`. |\r\n| `smape` | `mean(2 * \\|actual_i - predicted_i\\| / (\\|actual_i\\| + \\|predicted_i\\|)) * 100` | Skip samples where `\\|actual_i\\| + \\|predicted_i\\| < 1e-10`. Return 0.0 if no valid samples. |\r\n\r\n### 3.4 Bootstrap Confidence Intervals\r\n\r\nBootstrap confidence intervals provide uncertainty estimates for computed metrics. They are computed using the **percentile bootstrap** method.\r\n\r\n**Algorithm:**\r\n\r\n1. Let `N` be the number of predictions in a split and `B` be the number of bootstrap iterations (`--bootstrap` flag).\r\n2. Create a single PRNG instance seeded with `--seed` (default 42) using `math/ran"]
[1992.144114, "o", "d`. This single PRNG is shared across all metrics and all splits -- it is **not** reseeded per metric or per split.\r\n3. For each bootstrap iteration `b` in `[0, B)`:\r\n   a. Resample `N` predictions **with replacement** from the split's prediction array using the shared PRNG.\r\n   b. Compute all applicable metrics on the resampled set.\r\n4. For each metric, collect the `B` bootstrap values and sort them in ascending order.\r\n5. Compute the lower and upper percentile indices:\r\n   - `lower_index = floor((1 - confidence) / 2 * B)`\r\n   - `upper_index = floor((1 + confidence) / 2 * B) - 1`\r\n   - Clamp both indices to `[0, B-1]`.\r\n6. The confidence interval is `[sorted_values[lower_index], sorted_values[upper_index]]`.\r\n\r\n**Applicable metrics for CI computation:**\r\n\r\n| Task Type | Metrics with CI |\r\n|-----------|----------------|\r\n| `binary_classification` | `accuracy`, `precision`, `recall`, `f1`, `auc_roc` |\r\n| `multiclass_classification` | `accuracy`, `f1_macro`, `f1_weighted` |\r\n| `regression` | `mse`, `rmse`, `mae"]
[1992.14418, "o", "`, `r_squared` |\r\n\r\nNote: `log_loss` and `smape` do **not** get confidence intervals. Micro and per-class metrics do not get confidence intervals.\r\n\r\n**When `--bootstrap 0`:** Skip CI computation entirely. The `confidence_intervals` field must be omitted from the JSON output (not present as null or empty object).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 4. Report Format\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Evaluate Command Output\r\n\r\n**Markdown report** (`report.md`):\r\n\r\n```\r\n# Evaluation Report: <model_name> v<version>\r\n\r\nTask type: <task_type>\r\n\r\n"]
[1992.144239, "o", "## Summary\r\n"]
[1992.144733, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1992.144791, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[1992.407193, "i", "sed -n '241,330p' docs/spec_v2.md\n"]
[1992.407498, "o", "sed -n '241,330p' docs/spec_v2.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1992.410503, "o", "\r\n| Metric | <split_1> | <split_2> | ... |\r\n|--------|-----------|-----------|-----|\r\n| <metric> | <value> [<lower>, <upper>] | ... |\r\n\r\n(Metrics listed in the order defined for the task type. Values rounded to 6 decimal places. When bootstrap CIs are available for a metric, the value is shown as `<value> [<lower>, <upper>]` where lower and upper are the CI bounds rounded to 6 decimal places. When CIs are not available or bootstrap is disabled, only the value is shown.)\r\n\r\n## Split: <split_name>\r\n\r\n"]
[1992.410617, "o", "### Dataset\r\n<dataset_name>\r\n\r\n### Metrics\r\n\r\n| Metric | Value |\r\n|--------|-------|\r\n| <metric> | <value> |\r\n\r\n### Confusion Matrix\r\n\r\n(Classification only. Rows are actual, columns are predicted. Classes in lexicographic order.)\r\n\r\n|  | Predicted: <class_1> | Predicted: <class_2> | ... |\r\n|--|---------------------|---------------------|-----|\r\n| Actual: <class_1> | <count> | <count> | ... |\r\n| Actual: <class_2> | <count> | <count> | ... |\r\n\r\n### Per-Class Metrics\r\n\r\n(Multiclass only.)\r\n\r\n| Class | Precision | Recall | F1 | Support |\r\n|-------|-----------|--------|----|---------|\r\n| <class> | <value> | <value> | <value> | <count> |\r\n\r\n"]
[1992.410695, "o", "### Confidence Intervals\r\n\r\n(Only present when bootstrap is enabled, i.e., --bootstrap > 0. One row per metric that has CI.)\r\n\r\n| Metric | Lower | Upper |\r\n|--------|-------|-------|\r\n| <metric> | <lower> | <upper> |\r\n\r\n(Repeat \"## Split: ...\" section for each split, in the order they appear in the manifest.)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**JSON report** (`report.json`):\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"model\": {\r\n    \"name\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"version\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"task_type\": \"<string>\"\r\n"]
[1992.410834, "o", "  },\r\n  \"splits\": {\r\n    \"<split_name>\": {\r\n      \"dataset\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"metrics\": {\r\n        \"<metric_name>\": <float>\r\n      },\r\n      \"confusion_matrix\": {\r\n        \"classes\": [\"<class_1>\", \"<class_2>\", ...],\r\n        \"matrix\": [[<int>, ...], ...]\r\n      },\r\n      \"per_class_metrics\": {\r\n        \"<class>\": {\r\n          \"precision\": <float>,\r\n          \"recall\": <float>,\r\n          \"f1\": <float>,\r\n          \"support\": <int>\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"confidence_intervals\": {\r\n        \"<metric_name>\": {\r\n          \"lower\": <float>,\r\n          \"upper\": <float>\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[1992.410955, "o", "Fields that don't apply to the task type (e.g., `confusion_matrix` for regression, `per_class_metrics` for binary) are omitted from the JSON output entirely (not set to null or empty).\r\n\r\nThe `confidence_intervals` field is omitted entirely when `--bootstrap 0` is used. When bootstrap is enabled, it contains an entry for each metric that has CI computation (see Section 3.4). Each entry has `lower` and `upper` fields rounded to 6 decimal places.\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Compare Command Output\r\n\r\n"]
[1992.411428, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1992.411487, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2003.165936, "i", "grep -nE '^##|^###|Usage|Flags|evaluate|compare|Standard order|Rounding|Output Files|Confidence Intervals' docs/spec_v2.md\n"]
[2003.166752, "o", "grep -nE '^##|^###|Usage|Flags|evaluate|compare|Standard order|Rounding|Output Files|Confidence Intervals' docs/spec_v2.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2003.170222, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K3\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K Changes from v1\r\n"]
[2003.170507, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K7\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K2. **Extension -- Bootstrap \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KConfidence Intervals\u001b[m\u001b[K:** The `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevaluate\u001b[m\u001b[K` command now supports bootstrap confidence interval computation for all primary metrics. Three new CLI flags (`--bootstrap`, `--confidence`, `--seed`) control this feature. Confidence intervals appear in both JSON and Markdown reports.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K11\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K 1. Overview\r\n"]
[2003.170592, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K23\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K 2. Data Model\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K25\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 2.1 Evaluation Manifest\r\n"]
[2003.170669, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K75\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 2.2 Regression Configuration\r\n"]
[2003.170732, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K77\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KUsed with the `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kcompare\u001b[m\u001b[K` command to define regression thresholds and rules:\r\n"]
[2003.170795, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K108\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 2.3 Per-Metric Regression Evaluation\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K122\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K 3. Metric Computation\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K124\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 3.1 Binary Classification\r\n"]
[2003.170869, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K154\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 3.2 Multiclass Classification\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K185\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 3.3 Regression Metrics\r\n"]
[2003.170939, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K197\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 3.4 Bootstrap \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KConfidence Intervals\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K229\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K 4. Report Format\r\n"]
[2003.170997, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K231\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 4.1 Evaluate Command Output\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K240\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K Summary\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K248\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K Split: <split_name>\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K250\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K Dataset\r\n"]
[2003.171057, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K253\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K Metrics\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K259\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K Confusion Matrix\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K268\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K Per-Class Metrics\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K276\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KConfidence Intervals\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n"]
[2003.171122, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K329\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 4.2 Compare Command Output\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K340\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K Performance Delta\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K348\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K Regression Analysis\r\n"]
[2003.171188, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K356\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K Overall Verdict\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K399\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K 5. CLI Interface\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K401\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 5.1 Evaluate Command\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K404\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevaluate\u001b[m\u001b[K --manifest <path> --output-dir <path> [--format md|json|both] [--bootstrap <n>] [--confidence <level>] [--seed <int>]\r\n"]
[2003.171248, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K422\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 5.2 Compare Command\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K425\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kcompare\u001b[m\u001b[K --baseline <path> --candidate <path> --config <path> --output-dir <path> [--format md|json|both]\r\n"]
[2003.171306, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K448\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K###\u001b[m\u001b[K 5.3 Error Output\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K455\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K##\u001b[m\u001b[K 6. Numeric Formatting\r\n"]
