[2009.821112, "o", "### 4.1 Evaluate Command Output\r\n\r\n**Markdown report** (`report.md`):\r\n\r\n```\r\n# Evaluation Report: <model_name> v<version>\r\n\r\n"]
[2009.821203, "o", "Task type: <task_type>\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\n| Metric | <split_1> | <split_2> | ... |\r\n|--------|-----------|-----------|-----|\r\n| <metric> | <value> [<lower>, <upper>] | ... |\r\n\r\n(Metrics listed in the order defined for the task type. Values rounded to 6 decimal places. When bootstrap CIs are available for a metric, the value is shown as `<value> [<lower>, <upper>]` where lower and upper are the CI bounds rounded to 6 decimal places. When CIs are not available or bootstrap is disabled, only the value is shown.)\r\n\r\n## Split: <split_name>\r\n\r\n### Dataset\r\n<dataset_name>\r\n\r\n### Metrics\r\n\r\n"]
[2009.821241, "o", "| Metric | Value |\r\n|--------|-------|\r\n| <metric> | <value> |\r\n\r\n### Confusion Matrix\r\n\r\n(Classification only. Rows are actual, columns are predicted. Classes in lexicographic order.)\r\n"]
[2009.821481, "o", "\r\n|  | Predicted: <class_1> | Predicted: <class_2> | ... |\r\n|--|---------------------|---------------------|-----|\r\n| Actual: <class_1> | <count> | <count> | ... |\r\n| Actual: <class_2> | <count> | <count> | ... |\r\n\r\n### Per-Class Metrics\r\n\r\n(Multiclass only.)\r\n\r\n| Class | Precision | Recall | F1 | Support |\r\n|-------|-----------|--------|----|---------|\r\n| <class> | <value> | <value> | <value> | <count> |\r\n\r\n### Confidence Intervals\r\n\r\n(Only present when bootstrap is enabled, i.e., --bootstrap > 0. One row per metric that has CI.)\r\n\r\n| Metric | Lower | Upper |\r\n|--------|-------|-------|\r\n| <metric> | <lower> | <upper> |\r\n\r\n(Repeat \"## Split: ...\" section for each split, in the order they appear in the manifest.)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**JSON report** (`report.json`):\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"model\": {\r\n    \"name\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"version\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"task_type\": \"<string>\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"splits\": {\r\n    \"<split_name>\": {\r\n      \"dataset\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"metrics\": {\r\n        \"<metric_name>\": <float>\r\n      },\r\n"]
[2009.82156, "o", "      \"confusion_matrix\": {\r\n        \"classes\": [\"<class_1>\", \"<class_2>\", ...],\r\n        \"matrix\": [[<int>, ...], ...]\r\n      },\r\n      \"per_class_metrics\": {\r\n        \"<class>\": {\r\n          \"precision\": <float>,\r\n          \"recall\": <float>,\r\n          \"f1\": <float>,\r\n          \"support\": <int>\r\n        }\r\n"]
[2009.821625, "o", "      },\r\n      \"confidence_intervals\": {\r\n        \"<metric_name>\": {\r\n          \"lower\": <float>,\r\n          \"upper\": <float>\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n"]
[2009.821696, "o", "```\r\n\r\nFields that don't apply to the task type (e.g., `confusion_matrix` for regression, `per_class_metrics` for binary) are omitted from the JSON output entirely (not set to null or empty).\r\n\r\n"]
[2009.821756, "o", "The `confidence_intervals` field is omitted entirely when `--bootstrap 0` is used. When bootstrap is enabled, it contains an entry for each metric that has CI computation (see Section 3.4). Each entry has `lower` and `upper` fields rounded to 6 decimal places.\r\n\r\n"]
