[2037.983235, "o", "## 3. Metric Computation\r\n\r\n### 3.1 Binary Classification\r\n\r\n**Positive class convention:** The positive class is the class label that comes **last** in case-insensitive lexicographic order. For example, between `\"negative\"` and `\"positive\"`, `\"positive\"` is the positive class. Between `\"benign\"` and `\"malignant\"`, `\"malignant\"` is positive.\r\n\r\n"]
[2037.983336, "o", "**Confusion matrix** from raw predictions using the `predicted` field:\r\n- TP: `actual == positive_class AND predicted == positive_class`\r\n- FP: `actual == negative_class AND predicted == positive_class`\r\n- FN: `actual == positive_class AND predicted == negative_class`\r\n- TN: `actual == negative_class AND predicted == negative_class`\r\n\r\n**Metrics** (all rounded to 6 decimal places in output):\r\n\r\n| Metric | Formula | Division-by-zero handling |\r\n|--------|---------|--------------------------|\r\n| `accuracy` | `(TP + TN) / (TP + TN + FP + FN)` | Return 0.0 if denominator is 0 |\r\n| `precision` | `TP / (TP + FP)` | Return 0.0 if denominator is 0 |"]
[2037.983412, "o", "\r\n| `recall` | `TP / (TP + FN)` | Return 0.0 if denominator is 0 |\r\n| `f1` | `2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall)` | Return 0.0 if denominator is 0 |\r\n| `auc_roc` | Trapezoidal AUC over ROC curve (see below) | Requires at least one positive and one negative sample; return 0.0 otherwise |\r\n| `log_loss` | `-1/N * sum(y*ln(p) + (1-y)*ln(1-p))` | Clip probabilities to `[1e-15, 1-1e-15]` before log |\r\n\r\n**AUC-ROC computation:**\r\n\r\n1. Let `p_i` be the probability of the positive class for sample `i`.\r\n2. Sort all samples by `p_i` in **descending** order. Break ties by placing actual-positive samples before actual-negative samples (this ensures a consistent curve).\r\n3. Walk through sorted samples, tracking cumulative TP and FP counts.\r\n4. At each sample, compute `TPR = cumulative_TP / total_positives` and `FPR = cumulative_FP / total_negatives`.\r\n5. Compute AUC using the trapezoidal rule: `AUC = sum over consecutive points: (FPR_{i+1} - FPR_i) * (TPR_{i+1} + TPR_i) / 2`.\r\n6. Include the origin point `(0, 0"]
[2037.98348, "o", ")` at the start.\r\n\r\n### 3.2 Multiclass Classification\r\n\r\n**Class list:** Collect all unique class labels from `actual` values, sorted in case-insensitive lexicographic order.\r\n\r\n**Per-class metrics (one-vs-rest):**\r\nFor each class `c`:\r\n- TP_c: `actual == c AND predicted == c`\r\n- FP_c: `actual != c AND predicted == c`\r\n- FN_c: `actual == c AND predicted != c`\r\n- TN_c: `actual != c AND predicted != c`\r\n- Precision_c, Recall_c, F1_c computed as in binary.\r\n\r\n**Aggregate metrics:**\r\n\r\n| Aggregate | Definition |\r\n|-----------|------------|\r\n| `accuracy` | Total correct predictions / total predictions |\r\n| `precision_micro` | `sum(TP_c) / sum(TP_c + FP_c)` over all classes |\r\n| `recall_micro` | `sum(TP_c) / sum(TP_c + FN_c)` over all classes |\r\n| `f1_micro` | `2 * precision_micro * recall_micro / (precision_micro + recall_micro)` |\r\n| `precision_macro` | Arithmetic mean of per-class precisions |\r\n| `recall_macro` | Arithmetic mean of per-class recalls |\r\n| `f1_macro` | Arithmetic mean of per-class F1 scores |\r\n| `"]
[2037.98354, "o", "precision_weighted` | Weighted mean of per-class precisions, weighted by class support |\r\n| `recall_weighted` | Weighted mean of per-class recalls, weighted by class support |\r\n| `f1_weighted` | Weighted mean of per-class F1 scores, weighted by class support |\r\n\r\nWhere **support** for class `c` is the count of samples where `actual == c`.\r\n\r\nDivision-by-zero: return 0.0 for any metric where the denominator is 0.\r\n\r\n"]
[2037.984089, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
