[3734.420761, "o", "\t\t\tnp.Probabilities = probs\r\n   397\t\t\tnp.HasProbabilities = true\r\n   398\t\t}\r\n   399\t\treturn np, nil\r\n   400\t}\r\n   401\t\r\n   402\tfunc loadRegressionConfig(path string) (RegressionConfig, error) {\r\n   403\t\tvar cfg RegressionConfig\r\n   404\t\tif err := readJSON(path, &cfg); err != nil {\r\n   405\t\t\treturn RegressionConfig{}, err\r\n   406"]
[3734.420835, "o", "\t\t}\r\n   407\t\tfor metric, t := range cfg.Thresholds {\r\n   408\t\t\tswitch t.Severity {\r\n   409\t\t\tcase \"critical\", \"warning\", \"info\":\r\n   410\t\t\tdefault:\r\n   411\t\t\t\treturn RegressionConfig{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%s: invalid severity %q for metric %q\", path, t.Severity, metric)\r\n   412\t\t\t}\r\n   413\t\t}\r\n   414\t\treturn cfg, nil\r\n   415\t}\r\n"]
[3734.420907, "o", "   416\t\r\n   417\tfunc computeMetrics(taskType string, preds []NormPrediction) EvalResult {\r\n   418\t\tswitch taskType {\r\n   419\t\tcase \"binary_classification\":\r\n   420\t\t\treturn computeBinary(preds)\r\n   421\t\tcase \"multiclass_classification\":\r\n   422\t\t\treturn computeMulticlass(preds)\r\n   423\t\tcase \"regression\":\r\n   424\t\t"]
[3734.420966, "o", "\treturn computeRegression(preds)\r\n   425\t\tdefault:\r\n   426\t\t\treturn EvalResult{Metrics: map[string]float64{}, MetricOrder: metricOrderForTask(taskType)}\r\n   427\t\t}\r\n   428\t}\r\n   429\t\r\n   430\tfunc computeBinary(preds []NormPrediction) EvalResult {\r\n"]
[3734.421618, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[3734.421675, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[3734.72397, "i", "grep -n \"regression\\|Regression\\|max_delta\\|max_relative_delta\\|min_absolute_delta\\|min_relative_delta\\|direction\\|--split\\|split names\" docs/spec_v3.md\n"]
[3734.725109, "o", "grep -n \"regression\\|Regression\\|max_delta\\|max_relative_delta\\|min_absolute_delta\\|min_relative_delta\\|direction\\|--split\\|split names\" docs/spec_v3.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3734.728575, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K5\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K1. **Conflict -- Metric Direction-Aware \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KRegression\u001b[m\u001b[K Detection:** The `compare` command's \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K detection logic has been fundamentally changed to account for **metric \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K**. Metrics are now classified as either **higher-is-better** or **lower-is-better**. For higher-is-better metrics, \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K means the metric *decreased* (as before). For lower-is-better metrics, \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K means the metric *increased*. This replaces the v2 behavior where all metrics used the same comparison \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K (`delta < threshold`). See updated Section 2.3 for full details including the new threshold interpretation.\r\n"]
[3734.728705, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K7\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K2. **Extension -- Split Filtering:** The `evaluate` command now accepts a `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K--split\u001b[m\u001b[K` flag to evaluate only specified splits. Multiple splits can be specified as comma-separated values.\r\n"]
[3734.72877, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K14\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kclassification and \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K metrics, generates structured reports, and detects\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K15\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kperformance \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks between model versions.\r\n"]
[3734.728833, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K19\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K**multiclass classification**, and **\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K**.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K34\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \"task_type\": \"<binary_classification | multiclass_classification | \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K>\"\r\n"]
[3734.728906, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K57\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `model.task_type`: One of `binary_classification`, `multiclass_classification`, `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K`.\r\n"]
[3734.72897, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K63\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `predictions[].actual`: Ground truth label (string for classification, number for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K64\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `predictions[].predicted`: Model prediction (string for classification, number for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K).\r\n"]
[3734.729038, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K71\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- For \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K: `actual` and `predicted` must be numbers; `probabilities` must be absent or null.\r\n"]
[3734.729097, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K75\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K### 2.2 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KRegression\u001b[m\u001b[K Configuration\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K77\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KUsed with the `compare` command to define \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K thresholds and rules:\r\n"]
[3734.729181, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K83\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K\": <float>,\r\n"]
[3734.729362, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K84\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K\": <float>,\r\n"]
[3734.729424, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K89\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \"max_critical_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\": <int>,\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K90\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \"max_warning_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\": <int>\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K98\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`: Maximum acceptable absolute change in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K. This is always a non-negative number representing how much worse the metric can get. For higher-is-better metrics: the metric regresses if `baseline - candidate > \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`. For lower-is-better metrics: the metric regresses if `candidate - baseline > \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`.\r\n"]
[3734.729488, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K99\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`: Maximum acceptable relative change in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K as a non-negative fraction. For higher-is-better: `(baseline - candidate) / |baseline| > \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`. For lower-is-better: `(candidate - baseline) / |baseline| > \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`. When `|baseline| < 1e-10`, the relative check is skipped.\r\n"]
[3734.729552, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K102\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `rules.max_critical_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks`: Maximum number of critical-severity metrics that can regress. Exceeding this count -> overall FAIL.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K103\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `rules.max_warning_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks`: Maximum number of warning-severity metrics that can regress. Exceeding this count -> overall FAIL.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K104\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Info-severity \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks are reported but never cause overall FAIL.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K105\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- If a metric appears in evaluation results but not in `thresholds`, it is ignored for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K purposes.\r\n"]
[3734.729776, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K108\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K**Backward compatibility for config files:** If a threshold entry uses the old field names `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmin_absolute_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K` and `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmin_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K` (from v2), they should be treated as follows: `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K = -\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmin_absolute_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K` and `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K = -\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmin_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`. The tool must accept both old and new field names. If both old and new field names are present for the same threshold, the new names (`\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`, `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K`) take precedence.\r\n"]
[3734.729939, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K112\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KMetrics are classified by \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K:\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K119\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K### 2.4 Per-Metric \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KRegression\u001b[m\u001b[K Evaluation\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K125\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K   a. Determine the metric's \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K (Section 2.3).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K127\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      - `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K_delta = baseline_value - candidate_value` (positive means candidate is worse)\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K128\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      - The metric is regressed if `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K_delta > \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K` OR `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K_delta / |baseline_value| > \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K` (when `|baseline_value| > 1e-10`).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K130\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      - `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K_delta = candidate_value - baseline_value` (positive means candidate is worse)\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K131\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      - The metric is regressed if `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K_delta > \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K` OR `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K_delta / |baseline_"]
[3734.730014, "o", "value| > \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kmax_relative_delta\u001b[m\u001b[K` (when `|baseline_value| > 1e-10`).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K135\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K**Comparison report deltas:** In the performance delta table and JSON output, the `absolute_delta` field is always `candidate - baseline` (unchanged from v2). The `relative_delta` is `(candidate - baseline) / |baseline|` (unchanged from v2). The \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K awareness only affects the *\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K detection logic*, not the delta display.\r\n"]
[3734.730071, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K202\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K### 3.3 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KRegression\u001b[m\u001b[K Metrics\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K238\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K` | `mse`, `rmse`, `mae`, `r_squared` |\r\n"]
[3734.730127, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K301\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K(Repeat \"## Split: ...\" section for each split, in the order they appear in the manifest. When \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K--split\u001b[m\u001b[K is used, only the selected splits appear.)\r\n"]
[3734.730186, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K342\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KFields that don't apply to the task type (e.g., `confusion_matrix` for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K, `per_class_metrics` for binary) are omitted from the JSON output entirely (not set to null or empty).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K365\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K## \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KRegression\u001b[m\u001b[K Analysis\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K371\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K(Only metrics defined in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K config. Direction column shows the metric's \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K classification. If a metric did not regress on any split, verdict is PASS.)\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K376\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KCritical \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks: <count> / <max_allowed>\r\n"]
[3734.730249, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K377\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KWarning \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks: <count> / <max_allowed>\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K397\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K  \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K_analysis\": {\r\n"]
[3734.730307, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K400\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdirection\u001b[m\u001b[K\": \"<higher-is-better | lower-is-better>\",\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K407\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \"critical_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\": <int>,\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K408\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \"max_critical_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\": <int>,\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K409\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \"warning_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\": <int>,\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K410\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \"max_warning_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[Ks\": <int>\r\n"]
[3734.730367, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K422\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport evaluate --manifest <path> --output-dir <path> [--format md|json|both] [--bootstrap <n>] [--confidence <level>] [--seed <int>] [\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K--split\u001b[m\u001b[K <splits>]\r\n"]
[3734.730433, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K431\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K--split\u001b[m\u001b[K` (optional): Comma-separated list of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksplit names\u001b[m\u001b[K to include in the evaluation. Only these splits will be processed and appear in the output. If omitted, all splits in the manifest are processed. If a specified split does not exist in the manifest, exit with code 2 and an error message.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K449\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--config` (required): Path to \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K configuration JSON file.\r\n"]
[3734.730495, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K455\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Baseline and candidate must have the same set of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksplit names\u001b[m\u001b[K.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K463\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `0`: No \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression\u001b[m\u001b[K detected (overall PASS).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K464\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `1`: \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KRegression\u001b[m\u001b[K detected (overall FAIL).\r\n"]
[3734.731161, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[3734.731227, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[3758.51529, "i", "nl -ba main.go | sed -n '430,560p'\n"]
[3758.515613, "o", "nl -ba main.go | sed -n '430,560p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3758.519366, "o", "   430\tfunc computeBinary(preds []NormPrediction) EvalResult {\r\n   431\t\tclasses := collectClasses(preds, true)\r\n   432\t\tif len(classes) != 2 {\r\n   433\t\t\treturn EvalResult{Metrics: zeroMetrics(metricOrderForTask(\"binary_classification\")), MetricOrder: metricOrderForTask(\"binary_classification\"), ConfusionMatrix: makeConfusionMatrix(preds, classes)}\r\n   434\t\t}\r\n   435\t\tpos := classes[1]\r\n"]
