[4380.745463, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K5\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K1. **Extension -- `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` Subcommand:** A new `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` subcommand is added that reads an existing evaluation report (JSON) and outputs a concise, single-line \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K to stdout. This is useful for quick checks and CI/CD pipeline integration.\r\n"]
[4380.745623, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K255\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K## \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KSummary\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n"]
[4380.745707, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K413\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K### 4.3 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KSummary\u001b[m\u001b[K Command Output\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K415\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KThe `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` command reads a previously generated `report.json` file and outputs a concise single-line \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K to stdout.\r\n"]
[4380.745769, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K423\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K**\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KPrimary\u001b[m\u001b[K metrics** per task type (shown in order):\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K425\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| Task Type | \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KPrimary\u001b[m\u001b[K Metrics |\r\n"]
[4380.74587, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K431\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KFor each \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kprimary metric\u001b[m\u001b[K, the value shown is the **average across all splits**, rounded to 4 decimal places. If there is only one split, the value is simply that split's value (still rounded to 4 decimal places).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K492\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K### 5.3 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KSummary\u001b[m\u001b[K Command\r\n"]
[4380.745973, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K495\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K --report <path>\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K501\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Prints a single \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K line to stdout (see Section 4.3).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K518\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KSummary\u001b[m\u001b[K command metric values are rounded to **4 decimal places**.\r\n"]
