[4764.784214, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K1339\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kusage:\u001b[m\u001b[K mlreport <evaluate|compare|summary> ...\")\r\n"]
[4764.784694, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[4764.784819, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[4782.454476, "i", "grep -n \"smape\\|exclude-metric\\|bootstrap\\|regression CI\\|Regression CI\" docs/spec_v5.md\n"]
[4782.455245, "o", "grep -n \"smape\\|exclude-metric\\|bootstrap\\|regression CI\\|Regression CI\" docs/spec_v5.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4782.45882, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K5\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K1. **Correction -- Bootstrap CI for regression includes `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksmape\u001b[m\u001b[K`:** In previous versions, the `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksmape\u001b[m\u001b[K` metric was excluded from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K confidence interval computation for regression tasks. This has been corrected: `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksmape\u001b[m\u001b[K` is now included in the set of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression CI\u001b[m\u001b[K metrics. The full list of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression CI\u001b[m\u001b[K metrics is: `mse`, `rmse`, `mae`, `r_squared`, `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksmape\u001b[m\u001b[K`.\r\n"]
[4782.459002, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K7\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K2. **Extension -- `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kexclude-metric\u001b[m\u001b[K` flag for `compare` command:** A new `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kexclude-metric\u001b[m\u001b[K` flag has been added to the `compare` command. It accepts a comma-separated list of metric names to exclude from regression analysis. Excluded metrics are still computed and appear in the performance delta table, but they are not checked for regression and do not appear in the regression analysis table or JSON output. Non-existent metric names in the exclusion list are silently ignored.\r\n"]
[4782.459117, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K117\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| Lower-is-better | `mse`, `rmse`, `mae`, `log_loss`, `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksmape\u001b[m\u001b[K` |\r\n"]
[4782.459215, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K212\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksmape\u001b[m\u001b[K` | `mean(2 * |actual_i - predicted_i| / (|actual_i| + |predicted_i|)) * 100` | Skip samples where `|actual_i| + |predicted_i| < 1e-10`. Return 0.0 if no valid samples. |\r\n"]
[4782.459291, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K216\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KBootstrap confidence intervals provide uncertainty estimates for computed metrics. They are computed using the **percentile \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K** method.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K220\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K1. Let `N` be the number of predictions in a split and `B` be the number of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K iterations (`--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K` flag).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K222\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K3. For each \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K iteration `b` in `[0, B)`:\r\n"]
[4782.459371, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K225\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K4. For each metric, collect the `B` \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K values and sort them in ascending order.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K238\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `regression` | `mse`, `rmse`, `mae`, `r_squared`, `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksmape\u001b[m\u001b[K` |\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K242\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K**When `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K 0`:** Skip CI computation entirely. The `confidence_intervals` field must be omitted from the JSON output (not present as null or empty object).\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K263\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K(Metrics listed in the order defined for the task type. Values rounded to 6 decimal places. When \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K CIs are available for a metric, the value is shown as `<value> [<lower>, <upper>]` where lower and upper are the CI bounds rounded to 6 decimal places. When CIs are not available or \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K is disabled, only the value is shown.)\r\n"]
[4782.459433, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K295\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K(Only present when \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K is enabled, i.e., --\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K > 0. One row per metric that has CI.)\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K344\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KThe `confidence_intervals` field is omitted entirely when `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K 0` is used. When \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K is enabled, it contains an entry for each metric that has CI computation (see Section 3.4). Each entry has `lower` and `upper` fields rounded to 6 decimal places.\r\n"]
[4782.459509, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K371\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K(Only metrics defined in the regression config that are not excluded by `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kexclude-metric\u001b[m\u001b[K`. Direction column shows the metric's direction classification. If a metric did not regress on any split, verdict is PASS.)\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K415\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KNote: Metrics excluded by `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kexclude-metric\u001b[m\u001b[K` still appear in the `deltas` section but do not appear in the `regression_analysis` section.\r\n"]
[4782.459568, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K451\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport evaluate --manifest <path> --output-dir <path> [--format md|json|both] [--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K <n>] [--confidence <level>] [--seed <int>] [--split <splits>]\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K457\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K` (optional, default `1000`): Number of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K resampling iterations for confidence interval computation. Set to `0` to disable CI computation.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K458\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--confidence` (optional, default `0.95`): Confidence level for \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K intervals. Must be in `(0, 1)`.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K459\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--seed` (optional, default `42`): Random seed for the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kbootstrap\u001b[m\u001b[K PRNG.\r\n"]
[4782.459653, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K473\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport compare --baseline <path> --candidate <path> --config <path> --output-dir <path> [--format md|json|both] [--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kexclude-metric\u001b[m\u001b[K <metrics>]\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K481\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kexclude-metric\u001b[m\u001b[K` (optional): Comma-separated list of metric names to exclude from regression analysis. Excluded metrics are still computed and shown in the performance delta table, but they are not checked for regression and do not appear in the regression analysis table or JSON output. If a metric listed here does not exist in the evaluation results or regression config, it is silently ignored.\r\n"]
[4782.460167, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[4782.460252, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
