[5410.099567, "o", "grep -R \"buildComparisonMarkdown\\|runSummary\\|summary\\|regression analysis\\|sort.Strings\" -n .\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5410.104004, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./main.go\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K1185\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kfunc \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KbuildComparisonMarkdown\u001b[m\u001b[K(cd ComparisonData) string {\r\n"]
[5410.104162, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./main.go\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K1228\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\texcludeMetric := fs.String(\"exclude-metric\", \"\", \"comma-separated list of metric names to exclude from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K\")\r\n"]
[5410.104232, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./main.go\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K1298\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\t\tmd := \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KbuildComparisonMarkdown\u001b[m\u001b[K(cd)\r\n"]
[5410.104294, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./main.go\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K1334\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kfunc \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KrunSummary\u001b[m\u001b[K(args []string) int {\r\n"]
[5410.104379, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./main.go\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K1335\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\tfs := flag.NewFlagSet(\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K\", flag.ContinueOnError)\r\n"]
[5410.10444, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./main.go\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K1389\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"usage: mlreport <evaluate|compare|\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K> ...\")\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./main.go\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K1398\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\tcase \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K\":\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./main.go\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K1399\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\t\tcode = \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KrunSummary\u001b[m\u001b[K(os.Args[2:])\r\n"]
[5410.115464, "o", "grep: ./mlreport: binary file matches\r\n"]
[5410.1163, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v7.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K5\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K1. **Correction -- Regression analysis metric ordering in Markdown:** In v3-v6, the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K table in the compare command's Markdown output listed metrics in alphabetical order (using `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksort.Strings\u001b[m\u001b[K`). This was an oversight. Starting in v7, the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K table lists metrics in the **standard metric order** for the task type (the same order used in the evaluate output). For example, for regression tasks: `mse`, `rmse`, `mae`, `r_squared`, `smape`. For binary classification: `accuracy`, `precision`, `recall`, `f1`, `auc_roc`, `log_loss`. Only metrics that appear in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K are listed, but they follow the standard order rather than alphabetical. This change only affects Markdown output; JSON output uses object keys where order is not significant.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v7.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K7\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K2. **Extensio"]
[5410.116372, "o", "n -- `--json` flag for `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` command:** A new `--json` flag has been added to the `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` command. When `--json` is present, the command outputs a JSON object to stdout instead of the text \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K line. The JSON structure includes model information, split count, and primary metric values (averaged across splits, rounded to 4 decimal places). When `--json` is not present, behavior is unchanged (text line to stdout).\r\n"]
[5410.116491, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v7.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K421\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KThe `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` command reads a previously generated `report.json` file and outputs a concise \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K to stdout.\r\n"]
[5410.116558, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v7.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K520\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--exclude-metric` (optional): Comma-separated list of metric names to exclude from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K. Excluded metrics are still computed and shown in the performance delta table, but they are not checked for regression and do not appear in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K table or JSON output. If a metric listed here does not exist in the evaluation results or regression config, it is silently ignored.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v7.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K540\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K --report <path> [--json]\r\n"]
[5410.116623, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v7.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K544\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--json` (optional): When present, output a JSON object to stdout instead of the text \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K line. See Section 4.3 for the JSON structure.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v7.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K547\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Without `--json`: Prints a single \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K line to stdout (see Section 4.3).\r\n"]
[5410.116677, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v5.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K7\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K2. **Extension -- `--exclude-metric` flag for `compare` command:** A new `--exclude-metric` flag has been added to the `compare` command. It accepts a comma-separated list of metric names to exclude from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K. Excluded metrics are still computed and appear in the performance delta table, but they are not checked for regression and do not appear in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K table or JSON output. Non-existent metric names in the exclusion list are silently ignored.\r\n"]
[5410.116846, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v5.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K419\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KThe `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` command reads a previously generated `report.json` file and outputs a concise single-line \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K to stdout.\r\n"]
[5410.116921, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v5.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K481\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--exclude-metric` (optional): Comma-separated list of metric names to exclude from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K. Excluded metrics are still computed and shown in the performance delta table, but they are not checked for regression and do not appear in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K table or JSON output. If a metric listed here does not exist in the evaluation results or regression config, it is silently ignored.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v5.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K500\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K --report <path>\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v5.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K506\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Prints a single \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K line to stdout (see Section 4.3).\r\n"]
[5410.117145, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v6.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K421\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KThe `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` command reads a previously generated `report.json` file and outputs a concise single-line \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K to stdout.\r\n"]
[5410.117209, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v6.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K483\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--exclude-metric` (optional): Comma-separated list of metric names to exclude from \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K. Excluded metrics are still computed and shown in the performance delta table, but they are not checked for regression and do not appear in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kregression analysis\u001b[m\u001b[K table or JSON output. If a metric listed here does not exist in the evaluation results or regression config, it is silently ignored.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v6.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K503\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K --report <path>\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v6.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K509\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Prints a single \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K line to stdout (see Section 4.3).\r\n"]
[5410.117287, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v4.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K5\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K1. **Extension -- `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` Subcommand:** A new `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` subcommand is added that reads an existing evaluation report (JSON) and outputs a concise, single-line \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K to stdout. This is useful for quick checks and CI/CD pipeline integration.\r\n"]
[5410.117427, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v4.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K415\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KThe `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K` command reads a previously generated `report.json` file and outputs a concise single-line \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K to stdout.\r\n"]
[5410.11749, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v4.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K495\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlreport \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K --report <path>\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K./docs/spec_v4.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K501\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Prints a single \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Ksummary\u001b[m\u001b[K line to stdout (see Section 4.3).\r\n"]
